er-side redirect, like Stripe Checkout. See ",[507,1406,88],{"href":228},"\nand ",[507,1409,80],{"href":225}," for the full surface.",[536,1412],{},[539,1414,1416],{"id":1415},"feature-parity-and-whats-still-on-the-roadmap","Feature parity, and what's still on the roadmap",[469,1418,1419],{},"Vatly covers what a SaaS needs to start selling: subscriptions with trials, plan swaps,\ncancellation with grace and resume, one-off purchases, hosted checkout, refunds and chargebacks,\nand — because it's a Merchant of Record — VAT, invoicing and tax compliance handled for you. A\nfew capabilities you may use elsewhere aren't in the box yet. Here's the honest picture, and how\nto bridge it.",[544,1421,1422,1435],{},[547,1423,1424],{},[550,1425,1426,1429,1432],{},[553,1427,1428],{},"Capability",[553,1430,1431],{},"Vatly today",[553,1433,1434],{},"Notes",[570,1436,1437,1448,1460,1474,1483,1497,1513],{},[550,1438,1439,1442,1445],{},[575,1440,1441],{},"Subscriptions, trials, swap, grace, resume",[575,1443,1444],{},"✅",[575,1446,1447],{},"Full lifecycle, Cashier-shaped API",[550,1449,1450,1453,1455],{},[575,1451,1452],{},"One-off \u002F multi-item checkout",[575,1454,1444],{},[575,1456,1457],{},[473,1458,1459],{},"checkout()->create(items: …)",[550,1461,1462,1465,1467],{},[575,1463,1464],{},"VAT, invoicing, tax remittance",[575,1466,1444],{},[575,1468,1469,1470,1473],{},"Handled — it's the point of a MoR. With Cashier (classic Stripe Billing) this is ",[486,1471,1472],{},"your"," job.",[550,1475,1476,1478,1480],{},[575,1477,817],{},[575,1479,1444],{},[575,1481,1482],{},"First-class models + events (more than most provide)",[550,1484,1485,1488,1490],{},[575,1486,1487],{},"Test \u002F live segregation",[575,1489,1444],{},[575,1491,1492,1493,1496],{},"Every record carries ",[473,1494,1495],{},"testmode","; key prefix selects the mode",[550,1498,1499,1503,1506],{},[575,1500,1501],{},[491,1502,784],{},[575,1504,1505],{},"🔜 Roadmap",[575,1507,1508,1509,1512],{},"Until native codes land, model a promo as a dedicated ",[473,1510,1511],{},"subscription_plan_…"," at the discounted price and point that cohort at it. A couple of extra plans in the dashboard — not a blocker for launching offers.",[550,1514,1515,1519,1521],{},[575,1516,1517],{},[491,1518,801],{},[575,1520,1505],{},[575,1522,1523,1524,1526,1527,1530],{},"Vatly is built for SaaS, where entitlement follows subscription state — ",[473,1525,479],{}," ",[486,1528,1529],{},"is"," your license check. Per-seat keys for downloadable\u002Foffline software (Lemon Squeezy's signature feature) aren't here yet. If you ship license-activated desktop binaries, that's the one workflow to keep elsewhere for now.",[469,1532,1533],{},"The shape of the trade is deliberate: Vatly does the compliance-heavy core that's genuinely\nhard to build — being the seller of record, VAT across the EU, invoicing, disputes — and is\nfilling in the conveniences (coupons next) in the open. For a subscription SaaS selling into\nEurope and the world, there's enough here to launch today.",[536,1535],{},[539,1537,1539],{"id":1538},"why-teams-choose-vatly","Why teams choose Vatly",[469,1541,1542,1543,1546],{},"A Merchant of Record makes the tax burden disappear — it becomes the legal seller, so VAT,\ninvoicing and remittance stop being your problem. The real question is ",[486,1544,1545],{},"whose"," entity you hand that\nto, and that's where Vatly stands apart:",[1548,1549,1550,1556,1562],"ul",{},[853,1551,1552,1555],{},[491,1553,1554],{},"Europe-first, by design."," EEA-based, EU jurisdiction, customer data kept in Europe. The other\nMoRs sit in the UK (Paddle) or the US (Lemon Squeezy, Stripe Managed Payments) — jurisdiction is\nthe one axis that genuinely separates them, and the reason Vatly exists.",[853,1557,1558,1561],{},[491,1559,1560],{},"No exposure to US policy."," Your seller-of-record relationship and your customers' data stay\nunder EU law — a clean answer when an enterprise buyer, or your own board, asks where they sit.",[853,1563,1564,1567],{},[491,1565,1566],{},"One familiar API."," The Cashier-shaped surface means there's little to learn and little to\nrewrite.",[1569,1570,1571],"blockquote",{},[469,1572,1573],{},[491,1574,1575],{},"You Just Ship.",[536,1577],{},[539,1579,1581],{"id":1580},"next-steps","Next steps",[1548,1583,1584,1593,1601],{},[853,1585,1586,1589,1590,1592],{},[491,1587,1588],{},"Starting fresh"," → ",[507,1591,128],{"href":216}," wires up the trait, config, migrations and\nwebhook in a few minutes.",[853,1594,1595,1589,1598,1600],{},[491,1596,1597],{},"Already running another provider",[507,1599,241],{"href":242},"\nshows how to add Vatly beside your current biller and migrate customers over gradually.",[853,1602,1603,1589,1606,1608,1609,1608,1611,1608,1613,1608,1615,1608,1617],{},[491,1604,1605],{},"Reference",[507,1607,173],{"href":219}," · ",[507,1610,68],{"href":222},[507,1612,80],{"href":225},[507,1614,88],{"href":228},[507,1616,96],{"href":231},[507,1618,50],{"href":234},[469,1620,1621,1622,1625,1626,1625,1629,1632],{},"Compared against, at time of writing:\n",[507,1623,512],{"href":509,"rel":1624},[511]," ·\n",[507,1627,517],{"href":515,"rel":1628},[511],[507,1630,523],{"href":521,"rel":1631},[511],".\nTheir method names and table layouts follow those packages' current releases — verify against\nthe version you have pinned before relying on a specific signature.",[1634,1635,1636],"style",{},"html pre.shiki code .sbssI, html code.shiki .sbssI{--shiki-light:#F76D47;--shiki-default:#F78C6C;--shiki-dark:#F78C6C}html pre.shiki code .sTEyZ, html code.shiki .sTEyZ{--shiki-light:#90A4AE;--shiki-default:#EEFFFF;--shiki-dark:#BABED8}html pre.shiki code .sMK4o, html code.shiki .sMK4o{--shiki-light:#39ADB5;--shiki-default:#89DDFF;--shiki-dark:#89DDFF}html pre.shiki code .spNyl, html code.shiki .spNyl{--shiki-light:#9C3EDA;--shiki-default:#C792EA;--shiki-dark:#C792EA}html pre.shiki code .sBMFI, html code.shiki .sBMFI{--shiki-light:#E2931D;--shiki-default:#FFCB6B;